Package: forecastingtools
Type: Package
Title: Teaching-Oriented Tools for Forecast Evaluation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Miguel A.", "Arranz", email = "maarranz@eco.uc3m.es",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5951-2284"))
Description: Static (sequential one-step) ARIMA forecasting, forecast accuracy
    measures and tests of forecast performance, developed for Applied Time
    Series Econometrics (ATSE) at Universidad Carlos III de Madrid. R port of
    the Python package Forecasting-Tools. Provides mean errors and other
    accuracy measures, unbiasedness (mean-error and Mincer-Zarnowitz), weak
    efficiency and orthogonality tests, and the Morgan-Granger-Newbold,
    Diebold-Mariano (with the Harvey-Leybourne-Newbold correction) and
    forecast encompassing comparisons, with Newey-West (Bartlett) inference.
